    "file": "web/src/screens/MissionDetailScreen.tsx",
    "line": 55,
    "summary": "approveMutation and rejectMutation only invalidate the [\"mission\", missionId] query on settle, never [\"missions\"] (the list query MissionListScreen.tsx reads) — unlike MissionCreateScreen.tsx's createMutation, which does invalidate [\"missions\"] on success.",
    "failure_scenario": "A Director opens a mission in 'pending_approval', clicks Approve (api.mission.approve succeeds), then clicks 'All missions' to go back to MissionListScreen within queryClient.ts's 15-second staleTime (web/src/api/queryClient.ts:6). Because [\"missions\"] was never invalidated, react-query serves the cached list with the mission still shown as 'Pending approval' (wrong status badge and wrong count in the status filter chips) until the 15s staleTime lapses or a manual refetch occurs."
  },
  {
    "file": "web/src/screens/MyAssignmentsScreen.tsx",
    "line": 63,
    "summary": "respondMutation (accept/decline) only invalidates [\"assignments\"] on settle, never [\"mission\", missionId] for the affected mission, even though accepting an assignment changes that mission's confirmed headcount (services/mission.py's RequirementFulfillment.confirmed, exposed as MissionDetailOut.requirements[].confirmed).",
    "failure_scenario": "A Director has MissionDetailScreen.tsx open (or had it cached within the last 15s) for a mission with an open requirement. A crew member accepts a proposed assignment on that mission via MyAssignmentsScreen.tsx. Since [\"mission\", missionId] is never invalidated by the respond mutation, the Director's FulfillmentBar / 'Fulfillment' panel keeps showing the pre-accept confirmed count (e.g. '0/1' instead of '1/1') until that query goes stale or is manually refetched, even though the server-side headcount is already correct."
  }
